### V64-D4 — P2 — the harness's own comment stripper deletes real code after a bare CR

```
stripTS('// a comment\r\nconst x = 1;\r\n')  ->  'const x = 1;\n'
stripTS('// a comment\rconst x = 1;\r\n')    ->  ''          ← the code is gone, silently
```

A bare CR is a JavaScript line terminator; `_gate_extract.mjs` normalises `\r\n` only, so the comment
swallows the code and the whole line is dropped. **Every behavioural harness in this repo goes through
`stripTS`.** `index.ts` **already contains one bare CR** (offset 554776, ~line 6651) — harmless today
because it joins comment to comment, and invisible to the purity gate, which counts bare **LF** (0 of 6,977 ✓)
and says nothing about bare **CR**. Failure mode: *"the window silently loses a block and the suite passes
on code it never executed."* One-character fix: `s.replace(/\r\n?/g, '\n')`.

